interp-only: this fixture drives the session peer with an interpreter `async`
fiber, so it only runs under the cooperative session-channel runtime of
`tur --interpret` (tests/run-turi.sh).  The compiled suite (tests/run.sh) skips
it: under the compiled pthread session runtime a session op inside a
cooperative async fiber has no separate thread to rendezvous with.  See
docs/archive/turi-session-types-plan.md (Slice C).
